github.com/users/perchrh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perchrh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perchrh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perchrh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perchrh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-01-25T10:01:56Z","updated_at":"2016-01-25T10:01:56Z","body":"Those are good points about the spec. \nWhen PES packets are handled, the data alignment indicator (DAI) of the packet can be read, and the payloads aggregated until the next packet with DAI = 1 arrives. Then the data can be passed along, to have the ID3 data parsed. \nThere might be some part of the spec that says you must make sure to send a PES packet with DAI = 1 to end the final sequence of ID3 data, to address the mentioned edge case. The assumption that non-max size payload in a continuation PES packet mean that this is the last continuation packet, may be safe in practice. \nRegarding the waiting, I don't have any ideas, other than that yes, that seems like a shortcoming of the spec. If PES-packets are not allowed to span TS-files/chunks then the waiting would be less of an issue? I don't know if they are..\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/174457489/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"perchrh","id":222589,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjU4OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/222589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/perchrh","html_url":"https://github.com/perchrh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perchrh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perchrh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perchrh/gists{/gist_